[{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>For each of the following shapes, write an algebraic expression for the area, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the perimeter, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Square with sides of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Rectangle with sides of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Circle with radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Isosceles triangle with base of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and perpendicular height of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=4x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=2x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=6x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=\\pi x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=2\\pi x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"P=x+\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}2x+\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}2x=(1+\\sqrt{17})x.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>For each of the following 3D shapes, write an algebraic expression for the volume, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the total surface area, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Cube with sides of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Cuboid with sides of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x,x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Cylinder with radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and a length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Isosceles triangular based prism of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, with the triangle surface having base <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and a perpendicular height of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=6x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=3x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=4\\times3x^2+2x^2=14x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=\\pi x^2h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=2\\pi x^2+2\\pi xh\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=\\frac12x^2h,\\quad A=2\\times\\frac12x^2+xh+2\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac12x\\right)^2+x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=x^2+xh+\\sqrt5x^2=x^2+(1+\\sqrt5)xh.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>For each of the following, find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dV}{dr}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=20r-\\dfrac14r^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dP}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=\\dfrac1t+\\dfrac t2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dA}{dr}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=2r-\\dfrac{10}{r^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dC}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=\\dfrac{10}x+\\dfrac{x^2}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dV}{dr}=20-\\dfrac12r\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=t^{-1}+\\dfrac12t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dP}{dt}=-t^{-2}+\\dfrac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=2r-10r^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dA}{dr}=2+20r^{-3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=10x^{-1}+\\dfrac14x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dC}{dx}=-10x^{-2}+\\dfrac12x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Solve each of the following equations, leaving your answer in exact form:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25\\pi-4\\pi r^2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\dfrac{144}{x^2}+\\dfrac14=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\dfrac{10}{x^2}+\\dfrac12x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac14\\pi r-\\dfrac{27\\pi^2}{r^2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac15\\pi r-\\dfrac3{r^2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"25\\pi=4\\pi r^2\\Rightarrow25=4r^2\\Rightarrow r^2=\\frac{25}4\\Rightarrow r=\\frac52.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac14=\\frac{144}{x^2}\\Rightarrow x^2=576\\Rightarrow x=24.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12x=\\frac{10}{x^2}\\Rightarrow x^3=20\\Rightarrow x=\\sqrt[3]{20}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac14\\pi r=\\frac{27\\pi^2}{r^2}\\Rightarrow r^3=108\\pi\\Rightarrow r=\\sqrt[3]{108\\pi}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac15\\pi r=\\frac3{r^2}\\Rightarrow r^3=\\frac{15}\\pi\\Rightarrow r=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{15}\\pi}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>A rectangular enclosure is created within a field, with a wall forming one side with a width of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres. A rope of length 30 metres is used to form the remaining three sides.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q5.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> may be written as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=30x-2x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence, find the maximum area of the enclosure.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Length of enclosure: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30-2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Area: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=x(30-2x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dx}=30-4x\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dA}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"30-4x=0\\text{ so }x=\\frac{30}4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=30\\left(\\frac{30}4\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{30}4\\right)^2=\\frac{225}2=112.5\\text{ m}^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>The cost of a journey \u00a3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when a van when driving at a steady speed in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kilometres per hour may be modelled by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=\\frac{1156}v+\\frac v9+50\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the speed at which the minimum cost occurs.</p></li><li><p>Find the minimum cost.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=1156v^{-1}+\\frac19v+50\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dC}{dx}=-1156v^{-2}+\\frac19\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dC}{dv}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-\\frac{1156}{v^2}+\\frac19=0\\Rightarrow\\frac{1156}{v^2}=\\frac19\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac{v^2}{1156}=9\\Rightarrow v=102\\text{ kmh}^{-1}\\quad\\text{(must be positive).}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=\\frac{1156}{102}+\\frac{102}9+50=\\frac{218}3=\\pounds72.67.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>The diagram shows a solid cuboid with lengths <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q7.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The total surface area of the cuboid is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"100\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the volume may be written as</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=40x-\\frac{16}5x^3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Hence, find the maximum volume of the cuboid giving your answer to 1 decimal place.</p></li><li><p>Find the exact dimensions of the box for this maximum volume to occur.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Surface area: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"100=2xy+8xy+8x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{100-8x^2}{10x}=\\frac{10}x-\\frac{4x}5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Volume:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=4x^2y=4x^2\\left(\\frac{10}x-\\frac{4x}5\\right)=40x-\\frac{16}5x^3\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dV}{dx}=40-\\frac{48}5x^2\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dV}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"40-\\frac{48}5x^2=0\\Rightarrow\\frac{48}5x^2=40\\Rightarrow x^2=\\frac{25}6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\pm\\dfrac5{\\sqrt6}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> but <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a length.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=40\\left(\\frac5{\\sqrt6}\\right)-\\frac{16}5\\left(\\frac5{\\sqrt6}\\right)^3=54.433105\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=54.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (1 DP).</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=\\frac5{\\sqrt6},\\quad4x=\\frac{20}{\\sqrt6},\\quad y=2\\sqrt6-\\frac23\\sqrt6=\\frac43\\sqrt6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac5{\\sqrt6}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{20}{\\sqrt6}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac43\\sqrt6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The diagram shows an open-topped cuboid tank. Its base has width <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres and length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres and has a height of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q8.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>It is made from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"48\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of sheet metal.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the volume may be written as</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=16x-\\frac23x^3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Hence, find the maximum volume giving your answer to 1 decimal place.</p></li><li><p>Find the exact dimensions of the box for this maximum volume to occur.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Surface area: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"48=2xy+4xy+2x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{48-2x^2}{6x}=\\frac8x-\\frac x3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Volume:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=2x^2y=2x^2\\left(\\frac8x-\\frac x3\\right)=16x-\\frac23x^3\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dV}{dx}=16-2x^2\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dV}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"16-2x^2=0\\Rightarrow2x^2=16\\Rightarrow x^2=8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\pm2\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> but <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a length.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=16(2\\sqrt2)-\\frac23(2\\sqrt2)^3=\\frac{64}3\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=30.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (1 DP).</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=2\\sqrt2,\\quad2x=4\\sqrt2,\\quad y=2\\sqrt2-\\frac23\\sqrt2=\\frac43\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac43\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The diagram shows a plant pot which is a cylindrical container of radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm and height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm. The plant pot has an open top. The total surface area is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"48\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q9.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the volume may be written as</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=24\\pi r-\\frac\\pi2r^3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Hence find the maximum volume giving your answer in exact form.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Surface area: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"48\\pi=\\pi r^2+2\\pi rh\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h=\\frac{48\\pi-\\pi r^2}{2\\pi r}=\\frac{30}r+\\frac r2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Volume:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=\\pi r^2h=\\pi r^2\\left(\\frac{48}r+\\frac r2\\right)=24\\pi r-\\frac\\pi2r^3\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dV}{dx}=24\\pi-\\frac32\\pi r^2\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dV}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"24\\pi-\\frac32\\pi r^2=0\\Rightarrow\\frac32\\pi r^2=24\\pi\\Rightarrow r^2=16\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\pm4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> but <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a length.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=24\\pi(4)-\\frac\\pi2(4)^3=64\\pi\\text{ cm}^3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The diagram shows a piece of square cardboard with width 40 cm. Four squares are cut from the corners each of width <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm. The cardboard is then folded into an open tray.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q10.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find the maximum capacity of the tray. Give your answer to 1 decimal place.</p>","steps":["<p>Capacity of tray:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=x(40-2x)(40-2x)=4x^3-160x^2+1600x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dC}{dx}=12x^2-320x+1600\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dC}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"12x^2-320x+1600=0\\Rightarrow4(x-20)(3x-20)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\dfrac{20}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> but physically <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x\\ne40\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=4\\left(\\frac{20}3\\right)^3-160\\left(\\frac{20}3\\right)^2+1600\\left(\\frac{20}3\\right)=\\frac{128000}{27}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=4740.7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (1 DP).</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>A container is created as a closed cylinder with capacity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"432\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the dimensions of the container when its surface area is minimised.</p></li><li><p>For sealing the side of the container, a line of fluid is dropped along the length. Find the cost given it costs \u00a30.04 per cm.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Volume of container: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"432\\pi=\\pi r^2h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Surface area of container: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=2\\pi rh+2\\pi r^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=2\\pi r\\times\\frac{432\\pi}{\\pi r^2}+2\\pi r^2=\\frac{864\\pi}r+2\\pi r^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dr}=-864\\pi r^{-2}+4\\pi r\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dA}{dr}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-864\\pi r^{-2}+4\\pi r=0\\Rightarrow\\frac{864}{r^2}=4r\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow r^3=216\\Rightarrow r=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=\\dfrac{432}{6^2}=12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Cost for each container: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\times0.04=\\pounds0.48\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>The curve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=10-x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>and rectangle ABCD is shown in the diagram below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q12.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Given that the rectangle is bounded by the curve and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, find the maximum area that the rectangle can have.</p>","steps":["<p>Let the length AB be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so length AD is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Area is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=2x(10-x^2)=20x-2x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dx}=20-6x^2\\quad\\text{max when }\\frac{dA}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"20-6x^2=0\\Rightarrow6x^2=20\\Rightarrow x^2=\\frac{10}3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x=\\sqrt{\\frac{10}3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\text{ max area: }20\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{10}3}\\right)-2\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{10}3}\\right)^3=\\frac{40}3\\sqrt{\\frac{10}3}=24.3\\text{ units}^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>A container for ice cream desserts is being designed to use as little plastic as possible. It needs to have a volume of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"144\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The vendors of the ice cream would like it to be comprised of an open top semi-sphere with a cylinder with the same radius attached, and that it should have no base or top. The radius of the cylinder is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm and the length of the cylinder is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q13.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>A sphere of radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has volume <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac43\\pi r^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and surface area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\pi r^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the area of plastic used is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=\\frac23\\pi r^2+\\frac{288\\pi}r.\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Hence find the radius which minimises the area.</p></li><li><p>By calculating the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for this to be minimised, state an issue with the vendor's requirement.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Volume: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"144\\pi=\\pi r^2h+\\dfrac23\\pi r^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow144-\\frac23r^3=r^2h\\Rightarrow\\frac{144}{r^2}-\\frac23r=h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Semi-sphere plus side of cylinder area:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}A&amp;=2\\pi r^2+2\\pi rh=2\\pi r^2+2\\pi r\\left(\\frac{144}{r^2}-\\frac23r\\right)\\\\&amp;=2\\pi r^2+\\frac{288\\pi}r-\\frac43\\pi r^2=\\frac23\\pi r^2+\\frac{288\\pi}r\\text{ as req.}\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dr}=\\frac43\\pi r-\\frac{288\\pi}{r^2}\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dA}{dr}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac43\\pi r-\\frac{288\\pi}{r^2}=0\\Rightarrow\\frac43\\pi r=\\frac{288\\pi}{r^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac43r^3=288\\Rightarrow r^3=216\\Rightarrow r=6\\text{ cm}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=\\dfrac{144}{36}-\\dfrac{12}3=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so that means that the least amount of material needed would only be a semi-sphere.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>A cylindrical metal container which is closed at either end, has a capacity of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"500\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The metal used for the curved side costs 0.03 pence/cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The cost for the circular bottom and top costs 0.07 pence/cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the cost of the metals for making the container may be given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=\\frac7{50}\\pi r^2+\\frac{30}r\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the radius of the container and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the cost in pence.</p></li><li><p>Find the radius for the minimum cost and height for that cost.</p></li><li><p>Hence calculate the minimum cost of making one of these containers to the nearest pence.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Volume: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"500=\\pi r^2h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Costs:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}C&amp;=0.07\\times2\\pi r^2+0.03\\times2\\pi rh\\\\&amp;=\\frac7{50}\\pi r^2+0.06\\pi r\\left(\\frac{500}{\\pi r^2}\\right)=\\frac7{50}\\pi r^2+\\frac{30}r.\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dC}{dr}=\\frac7{25}\\pi r-\\frac{30}{r^2}\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dC}{dr}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac7{25}\\pi r-\\frac{30}{r^2}=0\\Rightarrow\\frac7{25}\\pi r=\\frac{30}{r^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow r^3=\\frac{750}{7\\pi}\\Rightarrow r=3.2429315622\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=3.24\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h=\\frac{500}{\\pi r^2}=15.33\\ldots\\text{ so }h=15.1\\text{ cm (3 SF).}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=\\frac7{50}\\pi(3.2429315622\\ldots)^2+\\frac{30}{3.2429315622\\ldots}=13.8763\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so minimum cost is 14 pence (to the nearest pence).</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>A solid triangular based prism is made from wood with a volume of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(500(\\sqrt2-1)\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The two triangular ends are isosceles triangles with base <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm and perpendicular height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm. The length of the prism is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm. The rectangular sides are painted with paint that costs \u00a30.02 per cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the triangular ends are painted with paint that costs \u00a30.04 per cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q15.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the slanted sides (not the base) have a total area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt2xy\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Show that the cost of painting the prism is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=\\frac{20}x+\\frac2{25}x^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Hence calculate the minimum cost of painting one of these prisms.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Length: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{x^2+x^2}=\\sqrt{2x^2}=\\sqrt2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Area: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2xy\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Area of two slanted sides: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt2xy\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>surface area ends: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>surface area sides:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt2xy+2xy=2xy(\\sqrt2+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Volume of prism: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"500(\\sqrt2-1)=x^2y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{500(\\sqrt2-1)}{x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Total costs:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=0.02\\times2x\\frac{500(\\sqrt2-1)}{x^2}(\\sqrt2+1)+0.04\\times2x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=20x^{-1}+\\frac2{25}x^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dC}{dx}=-20x^{-2}+\\frac4{25}x\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dC}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-20x^{-2}+\\frac4{25}x=0\\Rightarrow\\frac4{25}x=\\frac{20}{x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x^3=125\\Rightarrow x=5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=\\dfrac{20}5+\\dfrac2{25}\\times25=\\pounds4+\\pounds2=\\pounds6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>A part of a garden is going to be filled with two different types of decorative stones. The design is a quarter circle with radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Each rectangle has width <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres and length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres and is laid out as shown in the diagram.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q16.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>For the quarter circle, the stones will be 80% of the cost of the stones for the rectangular areas. The total perimeter is 16 metres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the cost may be given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=8px-\\left(1+\\frac\\pi{20}\\right)px^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for some cost \u00a3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> per metre<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Show that the length of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the maximum cost is occurs when</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=\\frac{80}{20+\\pi}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Calculate the area of the quarter circle and the rectangles separately for this value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Perimeter: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16=2x+4y+\\dfrac14\\times2\\pi x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Area of rectangles:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2xy=2x\\left(\\frac{16-2x-\\frac12\\pi x}4\\right)=8x-\\left(1+\\frac\\pi4\\right)x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Area of quarter-circle: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac14\\pi x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Cost:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=p\\left[8x-\\left(1+\\frac\\pi4\\right)x^2\\right]+0.8p\\times\\frac14\\pi x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=8px-\\left(1+\\frac\\pi4\\right)px^2+\\frac15\\pi px^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C=8px-\\left(1+\\frac\\pi{20}\\right)px^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dC}{dx}=8p-2\\left(1+\\frac\\pi{20}\\right)px\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dC}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"8p-2\\left(1+\\frac\\pi{20}\\right)px=0\\Rightarrow2\\left(1+\\frac\\pi{20}\\right)px=8p\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\left(1+\\frac\\pi{20}\\right)x=4\\Rightarrow x=\\frac4{\\left(1+\\frac\\pi{20}\\right)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{80}{20+\\pi}\\text{ m as required.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"8\\left(\\frac{80}{20+\\pi}\\right)-\\left(1+\\frac\\pi4\\right)\\left(\\frac{80}{20+\\pi}\\right)^2=6.31906734\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Rectangle total area is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6.32\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac14\\pi\\left(\\frac{80}{20+\\pi}\\right)^2=9.38606086\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Quarter-circle area is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9.39\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.35-q17","number":17,"question":"<h3>Prerequisite knowledge for Q17: Arc Length and Sector Area in Radians</h3><p>A toy slice of cake is being manufactured and can be modelled by a sector of a circle with radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The volume is to be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"350\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The angle of the sector is 0.7 radians.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.35/questions/diagrams/q17.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the surface area may be written in the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=\\frac{2700}r+0.7r^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Hence find the minimum surface area and the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which obtain this, giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Volume: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"350=\\dfrac12r^2\\times0.7h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=\\dfrac{1000}{r^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Surface area:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=2hr+0.7rh+2\\times\\frac12r^2\\times0.7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=2.7rh+0.7r^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=2.7r\\left(\\frac{1000}{r^2}\\right)+0.7r^2=\\frac{2700}r+0.7r^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dr}=-2700r^{-2}+1.4r\\quad\\text{stat pt when }\\frac{dA}{dr}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-\\frac{2700}{r^2}+1.4r=0\\Rightarrow1.4r=\\frac{2700}{r^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow r^3=\\frac{13500}7\\Rightarrow r=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{13500}7}=12.4473980\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=12.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=\\frac{2700}{\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{13500}7}\\right)}+0.7\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{13500}7}\\right)^2=325.369\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=325\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF).</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h=\\frac{1000}{r^2}=6.45420637\\ldots\\text{ so }h=6.45\\text{ cm (3 SF).}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]